  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting the social and economic resilience of women, girls, youths and school going children</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oak Foundation requested CAFOD to develop a proposal for a comprehensive project in which CAFOD will provide capacity strengthening and accompaniment support to Caritas Masvingo, Caritas Mutare, Caritas Chinhoyi, St Alberts Mission and Alfred Walters Hostel to promote resilience amongst vulnerable groups particularly women, girls, mentally challenged children, people with disabilities (PWDs), youths and school going children. The project will promote the protection of vulnerable groups as well as enhance their livelihood options, while mitigating the negative impacts of the El Nino induced drought in Rushinga &amp; Mt Darwin districts through school feeding programmes.</narrative>
  </description>
